{"articles":{"Ahmedabad":{"x":"Ahmedabad is the seventh largest city in India with a population of 8.5 million. Although it is the commercial hub of one of the most prosperous states of India, Gujarat, it's not the state capital, which is its twin city of Gandhinagar, 30 km (19 mi) to the north. Ahmedabad is a good example of contrast between the materialistic attitude and the spirituality of self-renunciation.","sights":[{"n":"Sabarmati Ashram","k":"see","d":"Residence of Mahatma Gandhi (1917–1930)","img":"GANDHI ASHRAM 03.jpg","ll":[23.06,72.58083],"q":"Q1410702"},{"n":"Sidi Saiyyed Mosque","k":"see","d":"Mosque in Gujarat, India","img":"Front view Sidi saiyad mosque ahmedabad.jpg","ll":[23.02694,72.58111],"q":"Q2032778"},{"n":"Sidi Bashir Mosque","k":"see","d":"Mosque in India","img":"Shaking Minarets.jpg","ll":[23.0277,72.6012],"q":"Q2669049"},{"n":"Jama Masjid, Ahmedabad","k":"see","d":"Mosque of Gujarat, India","img":"Jama Masjid, Ahmedabad 03.jpg","ll":[23.02382,72.58722],"q":"Q2758009"},{"n":"Teen Darwaza","k":"see","d":"Historical gateway in Ahmedabad, India","img":"Teen Darwaza 1880s.jpg","ll":[23.0242,72.58464],"q":"Q18752661"},{"n":"Sarkhej Roza","k":"see","d":"Mosque and tomb complex in Ahmedabad, India","img":"Sarkhej.JPG","ll":[22.99214,72.50457],"q":"Q15697211"},{"n":"Bhadra Fort","k":"see","d":"Fort in Ahmedabad, India","img":"Bhadra Fort in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, India - 1872.jpg","ll":[23.02361,72.58111],"q":"Q3544561"},{"n":"Gujarat Vidyapith","k":"see","d":"Major university in Ahmedabad, Gujarat","img":"Gujarat Vidyapith Ahmedabad.jpg","ll":[23.04455,72.56737],"q":"Q1475631"}]},"Begusarai":{"x":"Begusarai is a city of 250,000 people (2011) in the Mithila region of Bihar.","sights":[{"n":"Kanwar Lake Bird Sanctuary","k":"see","d":"Contains rare and endangered migratory birds and has a large oxbow lake.","ll":[25.61,86.14]}]},"Deulti":{"x":"Deulti is a popular picnic spot in the Howrah district of West Bengal, along the Rupnarayan River. It was also the residence of Bengali writer Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay for 12 years.","sights":[{"n":"Madangopal Jiu Temple","k":"see","d":"A 370-year old Hindu temple, locally known as Gopāler Mondir (the temple of Gopala, another name of Lord Krishna).","img":"Madangopal jiu temple, Mellak.jpg","ll":[22.4668,87.9057]},{"n":"Sarat Chandra Kuthi","k":"see","d":"The house of Bengali novelist Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay for twelve years. The house was constructed in 1923 by a local worker named Gopal Das.","img":"House of Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay - Western View - Samtaber - Howrah 2014-10-19 9791.JPG","ll":[22.47514,87.90699]}]},"Dubrajpur":{"x":"Dubrajpur is a town in the central region of West Bengal.","sights":[{"n":"Hetampur Rajbari","k":"see","d":"A palace built in the shape of a castle with 999 doors.","img":"Ranjan Palace of Hetampur in Birbhum district 08.jpg","ll":[23.78094,87.39425]},{"n":"Mama Bhagne","k":"see","d":"A large number of large sized rocks are found in the area. Two remarkable pieces of these rocks were known as Mama and Bhagne (maternal uncle and nephew).","img":"Mama Bhagne Hills and Temple 24.jpg","ll":[23.78576,87.37097]},{"n":"Pahareshwar Kali temple","k":"see","d":"Kali temple in Dubrajpur","img":"Mama Bhagne 1.jpg","ll":[23.78556,87.37056],"q":"Q18987940"}]},"Dudhwa National Park":{"x":"Dudhwa National Park, in Lakhimpur-Kheri District of Uttar Pradesh, adjacent to Nepal border, is one of the major projects for wildlife preservation in India. Spread over an expanse of approximately 811 km² of marshes, grasslands and dense forests, it is a home for over 38 species of mammals, 16 species of reptiles and numerous species of birds. It has two core areas: Dudhwa National Park and Kishanpur wildlife sanctuary.","sights":[]},"Kalyani":{"x":"Kalyani is a planned township in the Nadia district of West Bengal, India.","sights":[{"n":"Ishwar Gupta Setu","k":"see","img":"KALYANI SETU - panoramio.jpg","ll":[22.96736,88.40766]},{"n":"Palpara Temple","k":"see","d":"A char-chala temple with terracotta reliefs.","img":"Palpara Temple - South Facade - Nadia 2013-10-20 3676-3687 Archive.tif","ll":[23.05847,88.51695]},{"n":"Kalyani Picnic Garden","k":"do","d":"You can enjoy a day long picnic here. It is at the western end of Congress road that leads straight from Kalyani main station. Good for group picnics.","img":"Kalyani Picnic Garden - Kalyani - Nadia 2017-02-05 5189.JPG","ll":[22.98247,88.42391]},{"n":"Kalyani Stadium","k":"do","img":"Kalyani Stadium 10.JPG","ll":[22.9748,88.44867]},{"n":"Lake Park","k":"do","img":"Kalyani Lake 01.JPG","ll":[22.97251,88.44355]},{"n":"Sayyid Jamaluddin Mosque","k":"see","d":"Mosque in Hooghly, West Bengal, India","img":"Mosque at Adi Saptagram- 05769.jpg","ll":[22.96042,88.3698],"q":"Q56425688"},{"n":"Hangseshwari Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple in Bansberia","img":"Haneswari and Vasudev temples3.jpg","ll":[22.96432,88.39981],"q":"Q5648088"},{"n":"Basilica of the Holy-Rosary","k":"see","d":"Church in West Bengal, India","img":"Bandel Basilica, Hooghly (West-Bengal).jpg","ll":[22.91895,88.39519],"q":"Q2887171"}]},"Karnasuvarna":{"x":"Karnasuvarna, an archaeological site in Murshidabad, covers the ruins of the former capital of Bengal under Shashanka.","sights":[{"n":"Residency Cemetery, Babulbona","k":"see","d":"Cemetery in Baharampur, Murshidabad","img":"Residency Cemetery, Babulbona in Baharampur 13.jpg","ll":[24.09683,88.26414],"q":"Q31728764"},{"n":"Raktamrittika Mahavihara","k":"see","d":"Ruins of a Buddhist university.","ll":[24.0255,88.18624]}]},"Kathgola":{"x":"Kathgola is a small town north of Murshidabad, on the eastern bank of the Bhagirathi River, famous for the Kathgola Palace and the Jagat Seths.","sights":[{"n":"Kathgola Palace","k":"see","d":"Once the residence of the Dugar family, now a museum showcasing chandeliers, mirrors, furniture and other artefacts.","img":"Kathgola Palace at Murshidabad district.jpg","ll":[24.2076,88.26723]},{"n":"House of Jagat Seth","k":"see","d":"The Jagat Seths were a business family and were involved in the business of banking and money lending.","img":"House Of Jagat Seth Complex - Mahimapur - Murshidabad 2017-03-28 6165-6169.tif","ll":[24.20916,88.26223]},{"n":"Jafarganj Cemetery","k":"see","d":"About half a mile from the Hazarduari Palace is Jafarganj Cemetery. The Cemetery contains the tombs of the Nawab's Nazim, from Mir Jafar to Humayun Jah.","img":"Jaffarganj Cemetery at Murshidabad 02.jpg","ll":[24.20086,88.2645]},{"n":"Nimak Haram Deorhi","k":"see","d":"Nimak Haram Deorhi is the gateway to Mir Jafars palace. The palace lo longer exist but the entrance gate still stands.","img":"Jafarganj Palace Gateway - Lalbagh - Murshidabad 2017-03-28 6254.JPG","ll":[24.20216,88.26366]},{"n":"Tomb of Azimunnisa Begum","k":"see","d":"Azimunnisa Begum, was the daughter of Murshid Quli Khan. According to legend she was diagnosed with an incurable disease.","img":"Tomb of Azimunnisha Begum.jpg","ll":[24.19827,88.26496]},{"n":"Hazarduari Palace","k":"see","d":"Historical building of Murshidabad, West Bengal","img":"Hazar Duari palace.jpg","ll":[24.1869,88.26876],"q":"Q5687746"},{"n":"Katra Masjid","k":"see","d":"Mosque in India","img":"Katra Masjid panoramic view.jpg","ll":[24.18483,88.288],"q":"Q6377841"},{"n":"Fauti Mosque","k":"see","d":"Mosque in India","img":"The Fauti Masjid - panoramio.jpg","ll":[24.18597,88.28051],"q":"Q5438372"}]},"Kavalkinaru":{"x":"Kavalkinaru is a beautiful village in the state of Tamil Nadu. Here, all religious people live together as one family. The village is a 45 Min drive from Thirunelveli and a 30 min drive from Nagercoil, and has a well connected road network and rail network.","sights":[{"n":"St. Joseph Shrine, Panagudi","k":"see","d":"Church in India","img":"Saint Joseph Shrine.jpg","ll":[8.3169,77.5777],"q":"Q11165948"}]},"Kayamkulam":{"x":"Kayamkulam is a city and a municipality in district of the Indian state of Kerala. It is an ancient maritime trading centre and is almost equidistant from Alappuzha town and Kollam.","sights":[{"n":"Krishnapuram Palace","k":"see","d":"Palace and museum with exhibits about the Travancore kingdom. The palace was built during the 18th century by Travancore Maharaja Marthanda Varma.","img":"Krishnapuram Palace in 2021.jpeg","ll":[9.1503,76.5088]},{"n":"Azheekal Beach","k":"see","d":"Beach in Kollam district, Kerala, India","img":"Azheekkal palli beach panorama.jpg","ll":[9.1322,76.4641],"q":"Q18110004"},{"n":"Kandiyoor Sree Mahadeva Temple","k":"see","d":"9th-century Hindu temples complex in Kerala","img":"Kandiyur Siva Temple Tower.JPG","ll":[9.25306,76.52944],"q":"Q15077801"},{"n":"Oachira Temple","k":"see","d":"Ancient temple in South Indian state of Kerala","img":"ഓച്ചിറആൽത്തറ.jpg","ll":[9.136,76.5102],"q":"Q7073393"},{"n":"Evoor Major Sri krishnaswamy temple","k":"see","d":"Human settlement in India","img":"Evoor temple.JPG","ll":[9.2305,76.4818],"q":"Q15217094"},{"n":"Chettikulangara Devi Temple","k":"see","d":"Capital of Onattukara","img":"ChettikulangaraTemple.jpg","ll":[9.227,76.517],"q":"Q5094200"},{"n":"Thrikkuratti Mahadeva Temple, Mannar","k":"see","d":"Temple in India","img":"Trkkrutti temple,.JPG","ll":[9.25306,76.52944],"q":"Q13114016"},{"n":"Vethalan Kavu Mahadeva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Kerala, India","img":"Vethalan Kavu.jpg","ll":[9.13861,76.53806],"q":"Q7923739"}]},"Lohgad":{"x":"Lohgad, literally meaning the iron fort, is a hill fort located in the Pune District in South Maharashtra near the hill-station of Lonavala. The fort stands on the edge of the Sahyadri Range and lies between the Indrayani and Pavana river basins. Because of its strategic location the Lohagad Fort is often considered as the strongest and most famous Deccan forts.","sights":[{"n":"Bhaja Caves","k":"see","d":"Buddhist archaeological site consisting of 22 rock-cut caves dating back to the 2nd century BC. It is considered as the oldest Buddhist caves of the Deccan region.","img":"Bhaja Caves Entrance Side View.jpg","ll":[18.72778,73.48194]},{"n":"Bedse Cave","k":"see","d":"The Bedse Caves are a small 1st-century BCE Buddhist rock-cut cave complex near Kamshet in Maharashtra.","img":"009 Chaitya and Simple Columns (33651621136).jpg","ll":[18.72132,73.53506]},{"n":"Karla Caves","k":"see","d":"Cave complex in Karla, India","img":"KARLA'S CAVES.JPG","ll":[18.78333,73.47056],"q":"Q6372431"},{"n":"Lohagad","k":"see","d":"Fort in Pune district, Maharashtra, India","img":"View of Lohgad.jpg","ll":[18.70986,73.47641],"q":"Q6667935"},{"n":"Bhushi Dam","k":"see","d":"Dam in Lonavala, India","img":"Bhushi dam.JPG","ll":[18.7227,73.3965],"q":"Q18601901"},{"n":"Gates","k":"see","d":"Winding stairways and paths with sharp hairpin bends lead through the top of the fort."}]},"Madurai":{"x":"Madurai, formerly Madura, is the third-largest city in the Indian state of Tamil Nadu. It is on the banks of the river Vaigai and has been a major settlement for two millennia. It is one of the oldest continuously inhabited cities in the world.","sights":[{"n":"Gandhi Memorial Museum","k":"see","d":"This museum houses Gandhi's bloodstained dhoti and little else by way of artifacts.","img":"Gandhi museum, Madurai.jpg","ll":[9.92992,78.13859]},{"n":"Samanar Hills","k":"see","d":"These rocky hills are home to various Jain and Hindu monuments dating between the 2nd-century BCE and the 12th-century CE.","img":"Samanar Malai Caves, Madurai.jpg","ll":[9.92278,78.0472]},{"n":"Thirumalai Nayakkar Mahal","k":"see","d":"The remains of the palace of the 17th-century ruler Thirumalai Nayak who contributed extensively to the Meenakshi Temple.","img":"S-TN-23 Thirumalai Naicker Palace Madurai 1.jpg","ll":[9.91488,78.1243]},{"n":"Kazimar Big Mosque and Maqbara","k":"see","d":"This traditional mosque (masjid) is at the heart of Madurai city, within 500 m of the Periyar (Central) bus stand and within 1 km south east of the Madurai Railway…","img":"Kazimarbigmosque.JPG","ll":[9.91275,78.1142]},{"n":"Thiruparankundram Dargah","k":"see","d":"An Islamic dargah is at the top of the Thiruparankundram Hill, where the grave of an Islamic saint Hazrat Sultan Sikandhar Badushah shaheed Radiyallah Ta'al anhu, who…","img":"Panorama of Thiruparankundram Madurai.jpg","ll":[9.89,78.056]},{"n":"Keeladi excavation site","k":"see","d":"ASI Archaeological site in Tamil Nadu","img":"KeeladiExcavationCamp2.jpg","ll":[9.86307,78.18209],"q":"Q25551381"},{"n":"Narasingam Yoga Narasimha Perumal Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Narasingam (4).jpg","ll":[9.96682,78.1889],"q":"Q6965437"},{"n":"Thiru Aappanoor","k":"see","d":"Shiva Temple in Madurai district, Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Appudayar1.jpg","ll":[9.9305,78.1228],"q":"Q12984017"}]},"Nalanda":{"x":"Nalanda is the site of a famous Buddhist university or mahāvihāra in the Indian state of Bihar. The university complex is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.","sights":[{"n":"Xuanzang Memorial","k":"see","d":"Xuanzang, also known as Hiuen Tsang, was a 7th-century Chinese Buddhist monk and teacher.","img":"Hiuen Tsang memorial, nalanda 2.jpg","ll":[25.14497,85.45424]},{"n":"Nalanda Mahavihara","k":"see","d":"Ancient Hindu-Buddhist monastery in present-day Bihar, India","img":"Nalanda The Great Stupa.jpg","ll":[25.1368,85.44383],"q":"Q216243"},{"n":"Jal Mandir","k":"see","d":"Jain temple in Bihar, India","img":"Pawapuri - 001 Temple marking Mahavira's Passing (9243092471).jpg","ll":[25.09111,85.53861],"q":"Q24934619"},{"n":"Jain temple, Kundalpur (Bihar)","k":"see","d":"Jain temple in the state of Bihar","img":"Kundalpur Jain Temple Nalanda (cropped).jpg","ll":[25.148,85.44464],"q":"Q108148410"},{"n":"Excavated remains of Mahavihara","k":"see","d":"Remains of the stupa has terraces and smaller stupas. ₹600 for foreigners. The ticket office is just across the road from the entrance. Mind the beggars and shopkeepers.","ll":[25.13631,85.44542]},{"n":"Nalanda Archaeological Museum","k":"see","d":"The museum houses a significant collection of Pala and Mauryan statues. The six air conditioned (!) rooms show off stone and metal statues that were found during the…","ll":[25.13532,85.4487]}]},"Panchkula":{"x":"Panchkula is a city in Haryana.","sights":[{"n":"Open Hand Monument","k":"see","d":"Monument in Chandigarh, India","img":"Open Hand Monument in Chandigarh.jpg","ll":[30.759,76.8074],"q":"Q16854086"},{"n":"Kaushalya Dam","k":"see","d":"Dam in India","img":"Kaushalya dam, Pinjor, district panchkula , Haryana, India.JPG","ll":[30.7753,76.9146],"q":"Q18126675"},{"n":"Burail Fort","k":"see","img":"Burail fort, Front East side piller, Chandigarh.JPG","ll":[30.7075,76.76111],"q":"Q21933307"},{"n":"Chhatbir Zoo","k":"see","d":"Zoo in Chandigarh, India","img":"Chattbir Zoo Chandigarh Entance.JPG","ll":[30.6036,76.7928],"q":"Q5087827"},{"n":"Cactus Garden","k":"see","d":"This is the largest succulent botanical garden of Asia. Situated in the heart of the city of Panchkula, it covers a total area of 7 acres."}]},"Pandya Nadu":{"x":"Pandya Nadu consists of the homeland of the Pandya dyansty as well as the southernmost point of mainland India.","sights":[{"n":"Samanar Hills","k":"see","d":"Hills in Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Samanar Malai Caves, Madurai.jpg","ll":[9.92278,78.0472],"q":"Q12977948"}]},"Panskura":{"x":"Panskura, a town along the Kangsabati River in West Bengal, is famous for the state's \"Valley of Flowers\". It's a popular weekend getaway for Kolkata residents in spring.","sights":[{"n":"Khirai","k":"see","d":"A secluded village, often called the \"Valley of Flowers\" of West Bengal.","ll":[22.388,87.707]}]},"Payyanur":{"x":"Payyanur is a town on the Perumba river in Kannur District, in the Malabar region of Kerala, India.","sights":[{"n":"Ezhimala Hill","k":"see","d":"Mountain in India","img":"Ezhimala beach.JPG","ll":[12.03333,75.2],"q":"Q5423276"},{"n":"Madayi Kavu","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Madayikkavu Thiruvarkkad Bhagavathi Temple.jpg","ll":[12.03472,75.26143],"q":"Q6726567"},{"n":"Tahir Mosque","k":"see","d":"Mosque in India","img":"Tahir Mosque, Peyangadi, Kerala.jpg","ll":[12.0167,75.2597],"q":"Q16901030"},{"n":"Aneekkara Poomala Bhagavathi Temple","k":"see","d":"Human settlement in India","img":"Aneekkara temple.jpg","ll":[12.06095,75.2259],"q":"Q4761577"},{"n":"Ettikkulam Beach","k":"see","d":"Curvaceous palm fringed beach with rocky surroundings. Near Kannurgate of Naval Academy."},{"n":"Kandoth Juma Masjidh","k":"see","d":"Majestic white building in a sprawling campus"}]},"Pondicherry (union territory)":{"x":"Pondicherry, officially Puducherry, is a union territory in Southern India. It consists of four enclaves in three different states, which came under French occupation before they were peacefully handed over to India. Each enclave shares a mixed cultural heritage, combining its South Indian roots with a French colonial past.","sights":[{"n":"Arikamedu","k":"see","d":"Still digging arikamedu","img":"Arikamedu, Early Historic Site 03.jpg","ll":[11.90267,79.81993],"q":"Q2861278"},{"n":"Immaculate Conception Cathedral, Pondicherry","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Puducherry Immaculate Conception Cathedral 2.jpg","ll":[11.93299,79.83055],"q":"Q1659902"},{"n":"Basilica of the Sacred Heart of Jesus","k":"see","d":"Pondicherry","img":"Puducherry Sacred Heart Cathedral 2.JPG","ll":[11.92626,79.82704],"q":"Q810086"},{"n":"Ousteri Lake","k":"see","d":"Lake in Puducherry, India","img":"Ousteri lake a.k.a. Osudu lake (48918579507).jpg","ll":[11.955,79.745],"q":"Q64604953"},{"n":"Aayi Mandapam","k":"see","d":"Park monument","img":"Puducherry-Bharathi Park-Aayi Mandapam-WUS02289.jpg","ll":[11.9331,79.8342],"q":"Q20572068"},{"n":"Varadaraja Perumal Temple","k":"see","d":"ASI protected monument in Pondicherry","img":"Varadharajaperumal temple, Puducherry (1).jpg","ll":[11.94083,79.83],"q":"Q24938746"},{"n":"Kameeswarar temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Puducherry, India","img":"Kameeswarar temple (9).jpg","ll":[11.91453,79.75581],"q":"Q55615622"},{"n":"Our Lady of Lourdes Shrine","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Villianur shrine.jpg","ll":[11.91126,79.76066],"q":"Q4302697"}]},"Shornur":{"x":"Shornur (Shoranur) is a small railway town in Palakkad District, Malabar, Kerala, India. Shornur is three kilometers from Kalamandalam, a cultural centre where the dance forms Kathakali and Koodiyattam are performed.","sights":[{"n":"Abaya Pradhan Temple","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Thirumittakode Anchumoorthi Temple.jpg","ll":[10.78278,76.18417],"q":"Q4663603"},{"n":"Kanjilassery Maha Siva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Kerala, India","img":"കാഞ്ഞിലശേരി മഹാദേവക്ഷേത്രം.jpg","ll":[10.70932,76.24058],"q":"Q16134564"},{"n":"Panayur Palur Shiva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in India","img":"Palur Panayur Siva Temple.jpg","ll":[10.79276,76.30816],"q":"Q13113221"},{"n":"Nedumpura Kulasekharanellur Shiva Temple","k":"see","d":"Shiva temple in Thrissur district, Kerala, India","img":"Nedumpura Temple Main Srikovil.PNG","ll":[10.73464,76.26169],"q":"Q16136181"},{"n":"Kaithali Temple","k":"see","d":"9th century Hindu temples complex in central Kerala","img":"Kaithali.jpg","ll":[10.80751,76.18952],"q":"Q41135737"},{"n":"Kaikkulangara Devi Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu Temple in Thrissur district, Kerala","img":"KaiKulangara Devi Temple - Ayyappan Kovil.jpg","ll":[10.85519,76.27958],"q":"Q20577522"}]},"Tenhippalam":{"x":"Tenhippalam or Thenhippalam, or Chelari is a small village in Malappuram District, Kerala, India. The headquarters of the University of Calicut is situated here.","sights":[{"n":"Beypore Lighthouse","k":"see","d":"Lighthouse in Kerala","img":"ബേപ്പൂർ വിളക്കുമാടം 02.jpg","ll":[11.1583,75.8058],"q":"Q16137790"},{"n":"Mulanthuruthy Marthoman Church","k":"see","d":"Church in Kerala, India","img":"Mulanthuruthymarthomanchurch.jpg","ll":[11.175,75.9187],"q":"Q6933740"},{"n":"Mannur Mahadeva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu Temple in Mannur Kerala","img":"Mannur Siva Temple, Quilandy.JPG","ll":[11.15274,75.83247],"q":"Q16134614"},{"n":"Pazhayangadi Mosque","k":"see","d":"Mosque in Kondotty, Malappuram, Kerala, India","img":"Pazhangadi Mosque Kondotty.jpg","ll":[11.14894,75.96219],"q":"Q25587066"},{"n":"Chelari sea walk","k":"do","d":"Take a bus from Tenhipalam to Thazhe Chelari (3 km). Turn from the highway to the western road, cross the bridge and reach Thayyilakadavu Bus Stop."},{"n":"University river walk","k":"do","d":"Start from the majestic main gate of the university, walk past the seminar hall and guest house buildings. Turn right from the canteen towards the administrative blocks."}]},"Ujjain":{"x":"Ujjain is a city in the Malwa region of Madhya Pradesh in India. It is home to the Mahakaleshwar Temple, one of the 12 Jyotirlingas of India, and famous for the Hindu pilgrimage Kumbh Mela, gathering hundreds of millions of pilgrims every 12 years.","sights":[{"n":"Jantar Mantar","k":"see","d":"Like the Jantar Mantars in Delhi and Jaipur, this one is also built by Maharaja Jai Singh II in 1725.","img":"Sun Dial Ved Shala Ujjain.jpg","ll":[23.1713,75.7665]},{"n":"Mahakaleshwar Temple","k":"see","d":"One of the main attractions of Ujjain and one of the 12 Jyotirlingas. The Jyotirlingas are said to be the most sacred abodes of Shiva.","img":"Mahakal Temple Ujjain.JPG","ll":[23.18278,75.76833]},{"n":"Kal Bhairav Temple","k":"see","d":"The worship of the eight Bhairavas is a part of Saivite tradition and the chief among them is Kal Bhairav, believed to have been built by King Bhadresen, on the banks of…","img":"Kal Bhairav temple Ujjain.jpg","ll":[23.21817,75.76862]},{"n":"Siddhwat Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu Temple in Ujjain, Madhya pradesh","img":"Siddhwat Temple.jpg","ll":[23.22421,75.77707],"q":"Q39049186"},{"n":"Bhartrihari Caves","k":"see","d":"These caves are just above the bank of the Shipra near the temple of Gadkalika.","ll":[23.20409,75.76664]},{"n":"Durgadas Ki Chhatri","k":"see","d":"This distinctive monument glows like a small jewel in the surrounding lush landscape."}]},"Yadagirigutta":{"x":"Yadagirigutta is a Hindu pilgrimage site near Bhongir in West Telangana. It is often called the \"Tirupati of Telangana\" for its spiritual significance.","sights":[{"n":"Sri Lakshmi Narasimha Swamy Temple","k":"see","d":"The hilltop Hindu town that draws pilgrims to the town. The temple is dedicated to the god Narasimha, an Avatar of Vishnu.","img":"Yadagirigutta temple main Gopuram.jpg","ll":[17.5848,78.9442]}]},"Warangal (WL)":{"x":"Near the station: Warangal Fort (Building in India).","sights":[{"n":"Warangal Fort","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Warangal fort.jpg","ll":[17.95722,79.61444],"q":"Q7968796"},{"n":"Thousand Pillar Temple","k":"see","d":"12th century Hindu trikuta temple in Hanamkonda, Telangana (Shiva, Vishnu, Surya)","img":"Thousand Pillar Temple-Warangal.jpg","ll":[18.00376,79.5747],"q":"Q7797068"},{"n":"Bhadrakali Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Warangal, Telangana, India","img":"Bhadrakali Temple, Warangal.jpg","ll":[17.9949,79.5828],"q":"Q16342368"},{"n":"Warangal Museum","k":"see","d":"A museum in Warangal, Telangana, India","img":"2021 view of the Warangal Museum, Warangal, Telangana.jpg","ll":[17.99096,79.58848],"q":"Q19899110"},{"n":"Govinda Rajula Gutta","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Govindarajula gutta 02.jpg","ll":[17.9758,79.6044],"q":"Q5589875"},{"n":"Padmakshi Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple dedicated to Lakshmi","img":"Jain Tirthankara Reliefs at Padmakshi Gutta 03.jpg","ll":[17.99795,79.567],"q":"Q19894997"}]},"Banka Ghat":{"x":"Near the station: Didarganj Yakshi (Very early Indian stone statue).","sights":[{"n":"Didarganj Yakshi","k":"see","d":"Very early Indian stone statue","img":"Didarganj Yakshi statue in the Bihar Museum.jpg","ll":[25.57167,85.2625],"q":"Q5274083"}]},"Carmelaram":{"x":"Near the station: Bellandur Lake (Lake in the southeast Bengaluru).","sights":[{"n":"Bellandur Lake","k":"see","d":"Lake in the sout